From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sander van Deijck <sander@vandeijck.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:44:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: xhci-pci-renesas: don't wait for sysfs fallback when a
 ROM is present

When an external ROM is present but its status reports no result yet,
renesas_xhci_check_request_fw() still asks for renesas_usb_fw.mem and
falls back to the ROM if the file is missing. With
CONFIG_FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER_FALLBACK=y that request waits for a
user-space helper, and when the driver is loaded early in boot, before
anything answers firmware uevents, probe stalls for the 60 s fallback
timeout.

Since the ROM is a valid fallback, use request_firmware_direct() in that
case so a missing file fails immediately. Without a ROM, keep the
existing behaviour.

Seen on a Check Point L-72 (Annapurna Labs Alpine, uPD720201 with
external ROM): the firmware request took ~61 s before "fallback to ROM".
With the sysfs fallback disabled, it fails in ~6 ms and the controller
comes up from the ROM as before.

Signed-off-by: Sander van Deijck <sander@vandeijck.com>
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci-renesas.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci-renesas.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci-renesas.c
@@ -604,7 +604,14 @@ static int renesas_xhci_check_request_fw
 		return has_rom ? 0 : err;
 
 	pci_dev_get(pdev);
-	err = firmware_request_nowarn(&fw, fw_name, &pdev->dev);
+	/*
+	 * With an external ROM the controller runs without the file, so do
+	 * not wait for a user-space helper: a missing file should fail fast.
+	 */
+	if (has_rom)
+		err = request_firmware_direct(&fw, fw_name, &pdev->dev);
+	else
+		err = firmware_request_nowarn(&fw, fw_name, &pdev->dev);
 	pci_dev_put(pdev);
 	if (err) {
 		if (has_rom) {
